// Zed keymap
//
// For information on how to configure Zed, see the Zed
// documentation: https://zed.dev/docs/key-bindings
//
// The only thing here is making omp the agent you get by default. Zed has no
// setting for that — the agent panel opens whichever agent you used last, and
// falls back to its own on a fresh project — so the new-thread key is bound
// to omp instead. The new-thread menu (cmd-alt-shift-n) still offers every
// other agent.
[
  {
    "context": "AgentPanel",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-n": ["agent::NewExternalAgentThread", { "agent": "omp" }]
    }
  },
  {
    "context": "AcpThread",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-n": ["agent::NewExternalAgentThread", { "agent": "omp" }]
    }
  }
]
